Lets `ssh-keygen -K` download nothing from a FIDO2 key holding no resident
keys, rather than failing with "Unable to load resident keys: invalid
format".

CTAP 2.1's authenticatorCredentialManagement answers enumerateRPsBegin with
CTAP2_ERR_NO_CREDENTIALS when the key holds no discoverable credentials,
which libfido2's fido_credman_get_dev_rp hands back as
FIDO_ERR_NO_CREDENTIALS. OpenSSH 10.5p1's read_rks treats that as any
other failure, so a new key can't be told from a broken one. Here it's a
key with nothing to download, as sk_load_resident_keys already counts a
key that doesn't do credential management at all.

--- a/sk-usbhid.c
+++ b/sk-usbhid.c
@@ -1297,6 +1297,12 @@
 		goto out;
 	}
 	if ((r = fido_credman_get_dev_rp(sk->dev, rp, pin)) != 0) {
+		if (r == FIDO_ERR_NO_CREDENTIALS) {
+			skdebug(__func__, "device %s holds no resident keys",
+			    sk->path);
+			ret = 0;
+			goto out;
+		}
 		skdebug(__func__, "get RPs for %s failed: %s",
 		    sk->path, fido_strerr(r));
 		goto out;
